            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 41,
              "start": 41
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Souter, the legal issue is whether a loss to the plan that originates from an individual participant\u2019s account qualifies as a loss to the plan under ERISA section (a)(2)."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "United States",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e84af8b76a3f99ec010531d8476a3f3114cfeb26f959979e412335019fdd6bdc",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e84af8b76a3f-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Amicus United States argues that ERISA allows a participant to sue to recover losses to the plan caused by a fiduciary breach even when the losses are attributable to the participant\u2019s individual account."
      }
    ],
