  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e84af8b76a3f99ec010531d8476a3f3114cfeb26f959979e412335019fdd6bdc",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e84af8b76a3f-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The case concerns the interpretation of ERISA sections 502(a)(2) and 409 regarding restoration of any losses to a plan."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e84af8b76a3f99ec010531d8476a3f3114cfeb26f959979e412335019fdd6bdc",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e84af8b76a3f-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioner argues that the phrase \u201cany losses to the plan\u201d includes any diminution in value of defined contribution plan assets, regardless of how many participants are affected."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Gies",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e84af8b76a3f99ec010531d8476a3f3114cfeb26f959979e412335019fdd6bdc",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e84af8b76a3f-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Gies, respondent argues that section (a)(2) does not permit an individual claim."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Gies",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e84af8b76a3f99ec010531d8476a3f3114cfeb26f959979e412335019fdd6bdc",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e84af8b76a3f-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 39,
              "start": 39
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Gies, respondent argues that recovery of assets such as diamonds and any associated profits would be available under section (a)(3)."
      }
    ],
